Drops yarns are made from 65% Peruvian Highland wool and 35% superfine alpaca. It is a popular and high-quality yarn. They are warm, comfortable and with good shape stability. Color does not fade. The clothes made of these yarns are well worn and resistant to wear. The Alpaca wool gives softness and comfort. They are very good for kids, because they are soft and warm.

Alpaca is very soft, silky and long-lasting yarn. Alpaca fibers contain microscopic air pockets, providing great insulation and keeping you warm during the winter. These same air pockets allow for outstanding breathability, it helps keep you cool in the summer. Alpaca is fluffy, soft, warm and resistant from pilling. These yarns are non-alergical, so it is very good for kids and people who are allergic to wool.

This product was washed with natural, non – allergic eco detergent and is ready to wear.

Care instruction: Hand wash, 30 degrees C (85 degrees F); Dry flat; Iron at low heat; Do not bleach; Do not hang.

